        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ತ್ಯಾಜ್ಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತ್ಯಾಜ್ಯ — tyājya — \"waste matter; refuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾರ್ಖಾನೆಯ ತ್ಯಾಜ್ಯ ನದಿಗೆ ಹರಿಯುತ್ತಿತ್ತು. kārkhāneya tyājya nadige hariyuttittu. Waste from the factory was flowing into the river."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಘನ ತ್ಯಾಜ್ಯ (tyājya), solid waste; ಕಸ is the everyday word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತ್ಯಾಜ್ಯ (tyājya) is borrowed from Sanskrit tyājya, \"to be left, to be abandoned\" (Monier-Williams): what is thrown away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
